The position is 11.
The width is 1.
The start is 1.
The count is 9.
Repeat while position is more than count.
Subtract count from position.
Set width to width plus 1.
Set start to start times 10.
Set count to 9 times start.

The offset is position minus 1.
The number is start plus (offset divided by width).
The place is offset modulo width.
The places is width minus 1.
The value is number.
For every step from 0 to places.
The digit is value modulo 10.
If step is places minus place, show digit, break.
Set value to value divided by 10.
